BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 615.0 Tm (1. Purpose and scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 595.5 Tm (This policy sets out how inpatients at Riverside General Hospital are prepared for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 581.0 Tm (discharge, how their care is handed over, and how they are followed up afterwards. It) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 566.5 Tm (applies to all adult inpatient wards, including the Cardiology, Orthopedics, Oncology) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 552.0 Tm (and Maternity units. Pediatric discharges follow the separate policy PED-020, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 537.5 Tm (transfers to another hospital follow policy NUR-131.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 506.5 Tm (2. Discharge criteria) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 487.0 Tm (A patient may be discharged when all of the following are true:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 469.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 469.5 Tm (The attending physician has documented that the patient is medically stable for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 455.0 Tm (discharge.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 437.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 437.5 Tm (Vital signs have been within the patient's target range for at least 12 hours.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 420.0 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 420.0 Tm (The patient, or their caregiver, can describe their medicines, warning signs and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 405.5 Tm (next appointment using the teach-back method.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 388.0 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 388.0 Tm (A safe destination is confirmed: home, a family member's home, or a care facility) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 373.5 Tm (that has accepted the patient.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 356.0 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 356.0 Tm (Transport has been arranged, and the patient will not drive themselves after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 341.5 Tm (sedation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 322.0 Tm (Planned discharges should happen before 11:00 a.m. so that beds are ready for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 307.5 Tm (afternoon admissions. The hospital target is that at least 40 percent of discharges) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 293.0 Tm (are completed before 11:00 a.m.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 262.0 Tm (3. Discharge checklist) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 242.5 Tm (The discharging nurse completes the electronic discharge checklist in the patient) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 228.0 Tm (record. The checklist must include:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 210.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 210.5 Tm (Medication reconciliation, completed by a pharmacist for patients who take five or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 196.0 Tm (more regular medicines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 178.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 178.5 Tm (A written discharge summary, which must be sent to the patient's primary care) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 164.0 Tm (provider within 24 hours of discharge.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 146.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 146.5 Tm (Removal of intravenous lines and urinary catheters, unless the care plan says they) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 132.0 Tm (stay in place.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 114.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 114.5 Tm (Return of the patient's own medicines and valuables.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 97.0 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 97.0 Tm (Booking of all follow-up appointments before the patient leaves the ward.) Tj ET
0.45 g BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 40 Tm (Riverside General Hospital | Policy NUR-114 v3.2 | Page 1 of 3) Tj ET
