BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 689.0 Tm (4. Risk assessment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 669.5 Tm (Every patient is scored with the Riverside Readmission Risk Score \(RRRS\) on the day) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 655.0 Tm (before discharge. The score ranges from 0 to 20 and is calculated in the patient) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 640.5 Tm (record from the patient's age, the number of admissions in the past 12 months, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 626.0 Tm (number of chronic conditions, and whether the patient lives alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 608.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 608.5 Tm (Low risk: a score of 0 to 6.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 591.0 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 591.0 Tm (Medium risk: a score of 7 to 12.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 573.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 573.5 Tm (High risk: a score of 13 or above.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 542.5 Tm (5. Follow-up timelines) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 523.0 Tm (Follow-up depends on the risk level recorded at discharge:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 505.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 505.5 Tm (High risk: a follow-up phone call from a transition-of-care nurse within 48 hours,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 491.0 Tm (and a clinic visit within 7 days.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 473.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 473.5 Tm (Medium risk: a follow-up phone call within 72 hours, and a clinic visit within 14) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 459.0 Tm (days.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 76.0 441.5 Tm (Х) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 441.5 Tm (Low risk: a clinic visit or a telehealth appointment within 30 days if the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 88.0 427.0 Tm (physician requests one. No phone call is required.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 407.5 Tm (If a high-risk patient cannot be reached after three call attempts on two different) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 393.0 Tm (days, the nurse informs the patient's primary care provider and records the attempts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 378.5 Tm (in the patient record.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 347.5 Tm (6. Readmissions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 328.0 Tm (Any unplanned readmission within 30 days of discharge is reviewed by the Quality and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 313.5 Tm (Patient Safety Committee within 10 business days. The review checks whether the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 299.0 Tm (discharge criteria, the checklist and the follow-up timelines in this policy were) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 284.5 Tm (met. The hospital's target 30-day readmission rate is below 12 percent for every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.0 270.0 Tm (adult ward.) Tj ET
0.45 g BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 40 Tm (Riverside General Hospital | Policy NUR-114 v3.2 | Page 2 of 3) Tj ET
